dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.document.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.document
start body
framing record

# ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION document wave: REAL binary pack
# frame, replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope shortcut
# (`📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs`'s old `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real, fixed)
# then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes` (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches `write_str_lp`'s
# own wire exactly, the proven BARE `segment` form per the flow report's UPDATE §7 fix) are
# genuinely, fully described. Past that, `styles`/`images`/`blocks` are HOMOGENEOUS but
# variable-length repeated records — `blocks` additionally embeds a data-carrying tagged `DocBlock`
# union with recursive `List`/`Table`/`Quote` nesting — the `protocol-array-of-records`/
# `protocol-prim-ref-recursion` gap (`repeat`'s own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N
# from a count field", for an untagged homogeneous record; `Prim::Ref` unconditionally errors on a
# nested/recursive field): modeled as one opaque trailing `payload` chain, the same honest boundary
# every P1-P3 pilot's own nested/recursive payload uses. The real Rust
# `encode_document_snapshot_binary`/`decode_document_snapshot_binary` stays genuinely, fully
# structured (varint counts, per-field length-prefixes, real 8-byte LE `f64`s, a real per-variant
# tag byte for `DocBlock`) — round-trip tested independently by this facet's own tests, only the
# protocol DESCRIPTION stops at this boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
